%[text] %[text:anchor:T_DEF03274] # Computer Vision Basics
%[text:tableOfContents]{"heading":"Table of Contents"}
%[text] %[text:anchor:H_577C7603] ## Scripts
%[text] ### [Intro to Image Segmentation](file:Scripts/IntrotoImageSegmentation.m)
%[text:table]{"ignoreHeader":true}
%[text] | ![Image of 6 gears overlaid by k-means clustering segmentation. There are two orange gears, two blue gears, and two purple gears.](text:image:6d3f) | <p>**In this script, students will...**</p><p>$\\bullet${"altText":"\bullet"} examine three image segmentation methods. </p><p>$\\bullet${"altText":"\bullet"} work through step-by-step examples of applying image segmentation.</p><p>$\\bullet${"altText":"\bullet"} distinguish appropriate image segmentation technique based on scenario.</p> | <p>**Academic disciplines**</p><p>$\\bullet${"altText":"\bullet"} Robotics</p><p>$\\bullet${"altText":"\bullet"} Computer Vision</p><p>$\\bullet${"altText":"\bullet"} Image Processing</p><p></p> |
%[text] | --- | --- | --- |
%[text:table]
%[text] ### [Edge Detection Theory](file:Scripts/EdgeDetectionTheory.m)
%[text:table]{"ignoreHeader":true}
%[text] | ![Image of a ramp edge with a horizontal line drawn across.](text:image:2fd7) | <p>**In this script, students will...**</p><p>$\\bullet${"altText":"\bullet"} identify and describe the characteristics and sources of edges.</p><p>$\\bullet${"altText":"\bullet"} characterize edges in 1D and 2D.</p><p>$\\bullet${"altText":"\bullet"} detect edges amid noise.</p><p></p> | <p>**Academic disciplines**</p><p>$\\bullet${"altText":"\bullet"} Computer Vision</p><p>$\\bullet${"altText":"\bullet"} Image Processing</p><p>$\\bullet${"altText":"\bullet"} Medical Imaging</p><p> </p><p></p> |
%[text] | --- | --- | --- |
%[text:table]
%[text] ### [Edge Detection Applied](file:Scripts/EdgeDetectionApplied.m) 
%[text:table]{"ignoreHeader":true}
%[text] | ![Image of post-processed edge showing which sections are edge and which are not.](text:image:52a9) | <p>**In this script, students will...**</p><p>$\\bullet${"altText":"\bullet"} evaluate edge detection methods.</p><p>$\\bullet${"altText":"\bullet"} apply edge detection techniques.</p><p></p><p></p> | <p>**Academic disciplines**</p><p>$\\bullet${"altText":"\bullet"} Computer Vision</p><p>$\\bullet${"altText":"\bullet"} Image Processing</p><p> </p> |
%[text] | --- | --- | --- |
%[text:table]
%[text] ### [Region Segmentation](file:Scripts/RegionSegmentation.m) 
%[text:table]{"ignoreHeader":true}
%[text] | ![Flower outlined in white against green leaves, with a dashed yellow line highlighting a section. Demonstrates the graph-cut method.](text:image:5a22) | <p>**In this script, students will...**</p><p>$\\bullet${"altText":"\bullet"} explore region segmentation techniques.</p><p>$\\bullet${"altText":"\bullet"} compare and contrast including histogram, k-means clustering, and graph-cut segmentation techniques. </p><p></p><p></p> | <p>**Academic disciplines**</p><p>$\\bullet${"altText":"\bullet"} Computer Vision</p><p>$\\bullet${"altText":"\bullet"} Image Processing</p> |
%[text] | --- | --- | --- |
%[text:table]
%[text] ### [Optical Flow](file:Scripts/OpticalFlow.m)
%[text:table]{"ignoreHeader":true}
%[text] | ![The motion color intensity map of a robot, showing motion with bright and dark hues.](text:image:4b91) | <p>**In this script, students will...**</p><p>$\\bullet${"altText":"\bullet"} examine assumptions underlying optical flow theory.</p><p>$\\bullet${"altText":"\bullet"} implement optical flow algorithms for motion detection.</p><p>$\\bullet${"altText":"\bullet"} compare and contrast optical flow techniques.</p><p></p> | <p>**Academic disciplines**</p><p>$\\bullet${"altText":"\bullet"} Computer Vision</p><p>$\\bullet${"altText":"\bullet"} Image Processing</p> |
%[text] | --- | --- | --- |
%[text:table]
